---
// Obligation Tracking — the awareness surface for the Obligation record type.
//
// THIS SUPERSEDED THE OBLIGATIONS INBOX, which was deleted on 2026-09-17 once nothing was
// being read across from it. What it settled is recorded here and in checkpoint §26. It was
// right about the threading and wrong about the metaphor: it borrowed mail, and mail brings
// an Open/Seen pivot and a filing verb on every row. Neither survives contact with a
// standing duty. Nothing is owed to a feed, and a duty that is in force today is still in
// force tomorrow whether or not you looked at it — so "seen" never meant anything. The only
// completable thing is a to-do, and a to-do is an Action, which already has a status model.
//
// WHAT THE PAGE IS. Two halves, as TABS rather than stacked sections — they are peers, and
// stacking made the registry read as a footnote you scroll past. You are either asking what
// is happening (the feed) or what the project is signed up to (the registry):
//   1. THE FEED, itself in four views — All · Important · To-do · Pinned. Important and
//      Pinned also read the other way round, a pivot swapping the parent and the child.
//   2. THE REGISTRY, in the SAME TWO VIEWS setup step 5 offers — By category
//      (bcn-sw-obligations-tree) and By commitment (bcn-sw-chain-tree), both the wizard's
//      own components with mode="browse" so there is nothing to decide. Setup gets rename,
//      remove, add, drag and the editor drawer; this gets the same levels, the same cards
//      and the same requirement children, and no verbs. Expand and collapse survive,
//      because they navigate rather than decide. One component with a mode, for the same
//      reason BcnRegistryTree takes one: setup approves along these trees and this page
//      reads along them, so they must not be free to drift.
//
// ONE FIXTURE, BOTH HALVES (aligned 2026-09-15). Corrected here on 2026-09-18 — this
// docblock had gone on claiming the two halves run on DIFFERENT POPULATIONS (the feed on a
// 402-duty hand registry, the registry tab on the ITP pass) for three days after that
// stopped being true. Both now read the setup wizard's fixture: the ITP pass of 2026-09-14,
// 854 requirements and the 333 obligations drafted from them, each carrying the
// requirements it came from. The counts reconcile because there is only one population.
//
// WHAT ALIGNING COST, kept because it is still the state of the drafted data: the 402-row
// registry carried a notice window, a parameter conflict, a monitor-facing condition and
// commitment codes that this fixture does not, and it had 50 Notify duties where the
// drafting pass produced 3. So To-do is short and no deadline appears anywhere. That is the
// data, not a regression in the page.
//
// WHAT REPLACES STATUS. Nothing on this page renders a verdict — the team dropped the
// compliance-status model, and the registry itself contains no status vocabulary. An
// obligation holds no time; the EVENT does.
//
// THE FOURTH VIEW IS PINNED, and it took three tries. Built as Standing, removed
// 2026-09-15, restored as Ongoing 2026-09-16, replaced by Pinned 2026-09-17. Ongoing
// answered "what is in force right now" and had to AUTHOR which activities were under way
// to do it, because nothing in the fixture records that an obligation is currently live.
// Pinning does not close that gap, it stops pretending to: the reader names what they are
// watching, which is a claim this system can keep. The cost, stated plainly — the page no
// longer answers "what is on right now" for anybody, and that should be reversed the moment
// obligations carry in-effect conditions.
//
// WHAT THE SETUP WIZARD CHANGED (merged from origin/main, built 2026-09-14). The record
// shrank to six fields: Title, Class, Category/Subcategory, Description, Trigger and
// Requirements. Three of those reach this page. The row label is the TITLE — never the
// trigger, because a list labelled with triggers reads as a list of accusations
// rather than duties in force. The old `condition` field is now the TRIGGER, and it is what a classifier
// matches evidence against rather than a sentence for a human. Species and activities are
// DERIVED from a duty's requirements rather than stored, so nothing here treats them as
// facts about the duty. Gate is no longer a field at all — whether a duty waits on an
// approved plan is read off its requirements' actions.
//
// WHAT IS REAL: every obligation, class, title, description, trigger, phase, subject filing
// and requirement link is fixture data, and every predicate matching a duty to an event is a
// real match against it. WHAT IS AUTHORED, and marked on the page: the events themselves,
// the five trigger matches (stage 2 is not running), and which six duties the reader has
// pinned. Nothing uses Date.now(); see the fixed NOW in src/data/obligation-tracking.ts.
import AppShell from '../../layouts/AppShell.astro';
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import BcnTrackingShell from '../../components/bcn/BcnTrackingShell.astro';
import { STEP_GLYPH } from '../../data/setup-wizard';
---

